# S02: Foundation — Contract Freeze and Risk Retirement

## Origin

Backlog source: Habr article *«Как я CRM в шаверму продал»* — small-business automation
(CRM → WMS → ERP → integration → business rules) told through a shawarma stand.
Seven pillars extracted: **P1** scannable guest card + loyalty · **P2** event-grained purchase
ledger with per-line composition · **P3** analytics that expose invisible waste · **P4** stock /
recipes / consumption / reorder point · **P5** CRM×ERP forecasting · **P6** IF/THEN business
rules · **P7** idempotent, attribute-isolated referrals.

This sprint implements **none** of them. It exists because a codebase audit found seven
contradictions that eight downstream migrations would otherwise bake in permanently.

## Objective

Build zero user-visible features. Retire the mechanisms every later sprint rests on
(verified-actor resolution, exactly-once writes, a working plpgsql RPC convention, scheduled
execution, live-data-safe line uniqueness), reconcile the three ghost objects that already have
live writers, and force the two vocabulary contradictions to a written decision.

## Findings that motivate this sprint

| # | Finding | Evidence |
| - | ------- | -------- |
| 1 | `refund_process` is not a legal DB value | `orders_payment_status_check` @ `001:62` allows `unpaid\|paid\|refunded`; `status-management.ts:18` defines it; `refund.post.ts:86-89` writes `REFUND_REQUESTED:` into `orders.notes` instead |
| 2 | Role vocabulary split | S01/BRIEF say `BARMAN`; DB CHECK says `bartender`; `create-empty.post.ts:54` branches on `'barman'`, which `validateUserRole` can never return |
| 3 | Ghost table with a live writer | `transactions.post.ts:215` inserts into `transaction_items` — no migration creates it; the error is `console.log`ed |
| 4 | Ghost column with a live writer | `mark-items-ready.post.ts:103` writes `order_items.ready_at` — column does not exist |
| 5 | Ghost function with live callers | `menu.get.ts:123,:144` call `record_metric()`, which exists in no migration; both are `.catch(console.error)` |
| 6 | No line uniqueness, but 8 reads assume it | ~8 `.eq('order_id',x).eq('menu_item_id',y).single()` reads with no unique index behind them |
| 7 | No venue timezone | `getDateRanges()` buckets in UTC; weekday labels use the *server* locale. Every future shift/forecast number is wrong until fixed |

