## Track A Execution Findings (2026-08-14)

Grounded by a 59-agent parallel pass over T03-T07, each drift claim then adversarially verified.
Items that changed the migrations, and items the next sprints must absorb.

**Corrections that would have caused real failures:**

1. `transaction_items.order_id` must be **TEXT**, not UUID. `orders.id` is text (001:56) while
   `transactions.id` is uuid (001:93). The symmetric guess fails with 42804.
2. `order_items.order_id` and `menu_item_id` are both **NULLABLE**, so 030's unique index needs
   `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` or it enforces nothing on NULL-keyed rows.
3. T03's "INSERT via service role only" is **unwritable as an RLS policy** — `service_role` has
   `rolbypassrls = true` and never evaluates policies. Correct form: enable RLS, create no INSERT
   policy.
4. `record_metric` must be **SECURITY INVOKER**. As DEFINER it would be an unauthenticated public
   write endpoint: PostgREST publishes every `public` function, EXECUTE defaults to PUBLIC, and no
   migration 001-025 contains a single GRANT or REVOKE.
5. T06's backfill silently mutates `public.tables` via `trigger_update_table_occupancy_on_order_change`
   (023:113-116). Header now reads `Dependencies: 001, 023`.

**Measured facts that contradict the plan:**

6. **Zero duplicate order lines exist** (51 rows, 0 dup pairs, 0 NULL keys). The sprint's
   "highest-probability migration failure" was not a risk at all. S04 may widen the index safely.
7. All 24 `orders` rows had NULL `restaurant_id` before 029 — the .pd stated the post-condition
   without the pre-state.
8. `/api/transactions` **POST has no caller** (`pay.vue:442` is a GET), and 3 of its 5 declared
   payment methods abort before the line-item insert. The DoD item "a payment through
   /api/transactions persists line rows" was verified at the data layer instead, using the exact
   object literal from `transactions.post.ts:185-193`.
9. `mark-items-ready` **throws**, it does not swallow — `ready_at` is in the `.select()` projection,
   so the whole UPDATE 400s. "Mark All Items Ready" was a hard, user-visible no-op, now fixed by 027.

**Open items handed to later sprints (do not lose these):**

10. `computeFrontendStatus` (`status-management.ts:201-230`) has **no branch for `refund_process`**.
    After 028 such an order renders as `'new'`. Read-side gap — belongs to S02-T12 or S04-T10.
11. Two more sources hardcode the 3-value payment set and are now stale:
    `composables/useOrders.ts:33` and `supabase/migrations/README.md:148`. → S02-T08 / T12.
12. `chat/users.get.ts` branches on `visitor|officer|waiter|barman|chef|admin` and **never
    `bartender`** — the only value `profiles.role` can hold. Bartenders get an empty chat list.
    Live bug. → S02-T12.
13. `usePerformance` sends `metric: 'execution_time'` / `'error'`, but `record_metric` writes
    `'menu_api_execution_time'` / `'menu_api_error'`, and `performance.get.ts:31` matches with an
    exact `eq()`. The dashboard will read empty until one side is aligned.
14. `update_order_progress()` dereferences `NEW.order_id` on an `AFTER ... OR DELETE` row trigger.
    `NEW` is NULL on DELETE, so it does **not** error (verified empirically) — it silently updates
    nothing, leaving `orders.order_progress` stale after any line deletion.
15. FK shape is not uniform: `orders`/`menu_items`.restaurant_id are ON DELETE CASCADE,
    `venue_settings` is NO ACTION, and invariant 7's text omits the cascade. S03+ inherits
    NO ACTION. Deliberately not unified in S02.

**Sprint-level state:** `pnpm build` passes (exit 0). `pnpm test:run` **fails 12/12** — every test
errors with `You must provide a Promise to expect() when using .rejects, not 'undefined'`, i.e. the
undefined-`$fetch` harness this sprint's DoD already names. Pre-existing, unrelated to Track A,
and exactly what **S02-T14** exists to fix.

