## Execution Decisions (frozen — carry into S02-INVARIANTS.md at close)

- **Migration application method:** Supabase **MCP `apply_migration`** against project
  `okcqrarepnwrvomswovk` (reda-db, eu-central-1). Project was `INACTIVE`; restored 2026-08-13.
  Every migration applied twice; second run must raise NOTICE, never EXCEPTION.
- **Commit scoping:** explicit `git add <paths>` per task, **not** `git add .` — the REDA tree
  carries 10 unrelated modified files. Supersedes EXECUTION.ppm Prompt B step 7.
- **Sprint branch:** `s02-foundation-contract-freeze`, cut from `main` @ `23775f367`.
- **⚠ Ledger drift:** `apply_migration` records the remote version as a **timestamp**
  (`20260813155552`), not the local file prefix (`025`). Local numbering and
  `supabase_migrations.schema_migrations` therefore diverge for every migration applied this way.
  Consequence: a future `supabase db push` would see `025-030` as unapplied and try to re-run them
  — which is survivable only because every migration in this sprint is idempotent by mandate.
  **Do not switch application methods mid-sprint.** Record in S02-INVARIANTS.md at close.
- **Idempotency proof method:** 1st pass via `apply_migration`, 2nd pass via `execute_sql` with the
  same SQL — this tests DDL idempotency without writing a duplicate ledger row.

